bwk-spscan-sys vendored libsecp256k1 (STRIPPED)
================================================

This is a relocated/symbol-renamed copy of libsecp256k1 (prefix
bwkspscan_v0_1_0_, links = "bwkspscan_v0_1_0") stripped to ONLY what the two
light-client Silent Payments scan kernels need:

  bwkspscan_v0_1_0_silentpayments_recipient_scan_lightclient_spend_points
  bwkspscan_v0_1_0_silentpayments_recipient_scan_lightclient_spend_points_batch

These are wrapped by the byte-FFI shim in
src/modules/silentpayments/spscan_ffi.c (bwkspscan_scan_spend_points[_batch]),
the only entry points bwk calls.

The differential test (tests/differential.rs, "differential_byte_identical") is
the gate: this stripped copy must produce byte-identical scan output vs the
upstream reference. Re-run after any change:

  cargo clean -p bwk-spscan-sys && cargo test -p bwk-spscan-sys

The CLEAN rebuild is mandatory: cc does not track #included headers, so an
incremental build can leave a stale object and link outdated symbols.

What was removed
----------------

Modules (build.rs ENABLE_MODULE_* define dropped + src/modules/<name>/ deleted):
  ecdh        - the SP light-client path does its OWN ECDH via the internal
                ecmult (create_shared_secret_vartime -> ecmult, and the
                in-module ecdh_lockstep); the ecdh module public fn is unused.
  schnorrsig  - signing, unused.
  ellswift    - unused.
  recovery    - unused (was not enabled; dir removed).
  musig       - unused (was not enabled; dir removed).

KEPT modules:
  extrakeys   - REQUIRED. The SP path uses xonly_pubkey_save/load/cmp and the
                shim uses xonly_pubkey_serialize.
  silentpayments - the kernels themselves.

SP module (src/modules/silentpayments/main_impl.h) trimmed to the light-client
path. KEPT: the two entry points above plus the static helpers they reach
(create_shared_secret_vartime, sha256_init_sharedsecret, create_t_k,
ecdh_lockstep). REMOVED exported functions: sender_create_outputs,
recipient_scan_outputs (full-node), recipient_public_data_* (create/serialize/
parse/load/magic), recipient_create_label, recipient_create_labeled_spend_pubkey,
recipient_create_shared_secret, recipient_sort*, calculate_input_hash,
recipient_scan_lightclient (base), recipient_create_output_pubkey; and the dead
statics (create_shared_secret const-time, create_output_pubkey,
append_lightclient_candidate, sha256_init_inputs/_label). The matching extern
declarations and now-unused types (silentpayments_recipient,
recipient_public_data, found_output, label_lookup, public_data_magic) were
dropped from include/secp256k1_silentpayments.h.

secp256k1.c: the public ECDSA sign/verify/normalize/parse/serialize block plus
the rfc6979 nonce machinery was removed (ECDSA is isolated and unused by the
scan path); src/ecdsa.h and src/ecdsa_impl.h deleted and the
#include "ecdsa_impl.h" dropped.

Uncompiled files deleted (not reachable from the compiled TUs - build.rs
compiles only src/secp256k1.c, src/precomputed_ecmult.c,
src/precomputed_ecmult_gen.c, and the shim):
  src/tests*.c, src/bench*.c/.h, src/ctime_tests.c, src/testrand*, src/testutil.h,
  the SP/extrakeys tests_impl.h/bench_impl.h/tests_exhaustive_impl.h/vectors.h/
  bip352_*_test_vectors.json/Makefile.am.include, the precompute_ecmult*.c table
  generators (standalone main()), contrib/ (lax_der_* - test-only), examples/,
  doc/, sage/, tools/, ci/, .github/, wycheproof, cmake/, build-aux/, and the
  autotools/CMake build files (CMakeLists.txt, configure.ac, Makefile.am, etc.),
  plus src/asm/ (ARM .s, not used by the cc build).

KEPT (load-bearing, not obvious): contrib/ was fully removed because
lax_der_parsing is only used by upstream tests; precomputed_ecmult.c (~2.4M) is
the ecmult table and is REQUIRED.

Updating to a newer secp256k1
-----------------------------

Treat this as a re-strip, not a merge: drop a fresh upstream tree in, re-apply
the symbol rename (prefix bwkspscan_v0_1_0_) and the removals listed above, then
confirm the differential gate is green with a clean rebuild.
